WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.153 --> 00:00:03.382
Hey Conan here, You're
watching the 360 Live Pre-Show,

00:00:03.382 --> 00:00:06.420
and now we've moved
out to another exciting

00:00:06.420 --> 00:00:08.134
part of the office here
at Warner Brother's.

00:00:08.134 --> 00:00:11.406
This is my assistant
Sona Movsesian's area.

00:00:11.406 --> 00:00:12.306
Hi Sona.
Hello.

00:00:12.306 --> 00:00:13.139
How are you?

00:00:13.139 --> 00:00:14.262
I'm doing well thank you, how are you?

00:00:14.262 --> 00:00:15.403
You and I've been together how many years,

00:00:15.403 --> 00:00:16.236
like two years?

00:00:16.236 --> 00:00:17.069
How long has it been?

00:00:17.069 --> 00:00:17.939
About eight.

00:00:17.939 --> 00:00:19.219
Eight. Two, eight.

00:00:19.219 --> 00:00:20.052
Close enough.

00:00:20.052 --> 00:00:20.885
Big difference.

00:00:20.885 --> 00:00:22.972
Probably moving on soon.

00:00:22.972 --> 00:00:23.805
Anyway.

00:00:24.697 --> 00:00:25.756
Sona's great.

00:00:25.756 --> 00:00:28.923
Sona and I are like peanut butter and,

00:00:29.893 --> 00:00:30.877
what?

00:00:30.877 --> 00:00:31.810
What are we like?

00:00:31.810 --> 00:00:33.205
Not like jelly, cause go well together.

00:00:33.205 --> 00:00:36.105
No, peanut butter, and like sauerkraut.

00:00:36.105 --> 00:00:38.162
Yeah, with asbestos in it.

00:00:38.162 --> 00:00:39.487
But it's whatever.

00:00:39.487 --> 00:00:42.754
And we can see what Sona's
working on right here.

00:00:42.754 --> 00:00:46.571
She's got the New York
Times crossword puzzle

00:00:46.571 --> 00:00:48.500
that she works on everyday.

00:00:48.500 --> 00:00:51.651
I usually say, hey Sona
this is really important.

00:00:51.651 --> 00:00:54.202
I need this done really
quickly, it's about the show.

00:00:54.202 --> 00:00:56.861
And she says I gotta
finish my New York Times.

00:00:56.861 --> 00:00:57.901
And then, what else?

00:00:57.901 --> 00:00:58.734
Oh!

00:00:58.734 --> 00:00:59.700
And then Sudoku.

00:00:59.700 --> 00:01:00.707
You do Su-doo-ko?

00:01:00.707 --> 00:01:01.540
Soo-do-ku?

00:01:01.540 --> 00:01:02.373
Sudoku.

00:01:02.373 --> 00:01:03.458
Everyday, and how does Sudoku work?

00:01:03.458 --> 00:01:04.374
I don't even know.

00:01:04.374 --> 00:01:06.515
Well, Sudoku you just have to have,

00:01:06.515 --> 00:01:10.057
you can't repeat the numbers
in the same row, column or box.

00:01:10.057 --> 00:01:13.395
And I do the easy level,
medium level, and hard level.

00:01:13.395 --> 00:01:14.228
Good for you.

00:01:14.228 --> 00:01:15.411
Thank you very much.

00:01:15.411 --> 00:01:17.044
Does it ever get in the way of work?

00:01:17.044 --> 00:01:17.877
Probably a lot?

00:01:17.877 --> 00:01:20.407
Yeah, quite a bit
Quite a bit, okay.

00:01:20.407 --> 00:01:22.429
And then this your desk area.

00:01:22.429 --> 00:01:24.630
It's actually cleaner than
when I've seen usually.

00:01:24.630 --> 00:01:26.317
You have a lot of Conan stuff here.

00:01:26.317 --> 00:01:29.465
Although I found out that this
was a Joel McHale bobble head

00:01:29.465 --> 00:01:33.165
that some fan turned into a
Conan O'Brien bobble head.

00:01:33.165 --> 00:01:34.477
I've never made this pose.

00:01:34.477 --> 00:01:35.547
Why?

00:01:35.547 --> 00:01:39.170
That is so rude to take
someone else's bobble head.

00:01:39.170 --> 00:01:40.712
Lots of Conan dolls.

00:01:40.712 --> 00:01:42.684
I don't know how to feel about this one.

00:01:42.684 --> 00:01:43.802
This is the one that reflects me

00:01:43.802 --> 00:01:45.127
probably the most accurately, right?

00:01:45.127 --> 00:01:45.960
Yes.

00:01:45.960 --> 00:01:46.793
Very pale.

00:01:46.793 --> 00:01:48.061
Very pale.

00:01:48.061 --> 00:01:49.348
Okay, take it easy.

00:01:49.348 --> 00:01:50.181
That's good.

00:01:50.181 --> 00:01:51.014
Lots of fun stuff.

00:01:51.014 --> 00:01:54.523
This is a picture of Sona
when you were, remember?

00:01:54.523 --> 00:01:56.267
When you were young, and
you were a ballerina?

00:01:56.267 --> 00:01:57.100
Yes.

00:01:57.100 --> 00:01:58.113
You look really nice and happy there.

00:01:58.113 --> 00:01:59.197
What happened?

00:01:59.197 --> 00:02:00.197
I grew up.

00:02:03.452 --> 00:02:05.352
Let's take a look at other things here.

00:02:05.352 --> 00:02:07.052
I'm just looking around your desk.

00:02:07.052 --> 00:02:10.956
You've got a Dwight Schrute bobble head.

00:02:10.956 --> 00:02:13.398
Again, that can easily be
converted into a Conan bobble head

00:02:13.398 --> 00:02:17.013
if you just make some
simple cosmetic changes.

00:02:17.013 --> 00:02:18.298
What are you drinking today?

00:02:18.298 --> 00:02:20.333
Well there's usually is water in that.

00:02:20.333 --> 00:02:22.123
But what else do you have during the day?

00:02:22.123 --> 00:02:25.201
Have you ever had alcohol
during the show days,

00:02:25.201 --> 00:02:28.061
like when you're working?

00:02:28.061 --> 00:02:28.894
Yes, yes.

00:02:28.894 --> 00:02:30.791
What did you have?

00:02:30.791 --> 00:02:34.389
Well, like a few days
ago we had some champagne

00:02:34.389 --> 00:02:35.942
with some St. Germain in it.

00:02:35.942 --> 00:02:37.091
Which was, I never.

00:02:37.091 --> 00:02:39.600
You had champagne during the day?

00:02:39.600 --> 00:02:40.720
Yeah I mean you know.

00:02:40.720 --> 00:02:42.566
It was just kind of a chill day.

00:02:42.566 --> 00:02:44.287
So we call it Juice-Juice Time.

00:02:44.287 --> 00:02:45.254
Juice-Juice Time.

00:02:45.254 --> 00:02:46.393
That's terrific Sona.

00:02:46.393 --> 00:02:48.151
Oh and look.

00:02:48.151 --> 00:02:48.984
This is great.

00:02:48.984 --> 00:02:50.451
This is a great sign for someone

00:02:50.451 --> 00:02:53.618
who drinks alcohol at work to have up.

00:02:54.986 --> 00:02:56.310
Oh look there's some pictures.

00:02:56.310 --> 00:02:58.352
There's me choking you with my tie.

00:02:58.352 --> 00:03:00.398
It's nice to have that framed.

00:03:00.398 --> 00:03:03.198
There's me and remember
when I introduced you to

00:03:03.198 --> 00:03:06.262
President Jimmy Carter and
Rosalynn Carter, the First Lady?

00:03:06.262 --> 00:03:07.575
Yes I do remember that.

00:03:07.575 --> 00:03:08.566
There's a photo.

00:03:08.566 --> 00:03:09.399
Yeah.

00:03:09.399 --> 00:03:10.706
It was a pretty big day for you, right?

00:03:10.706 --> 00:03:12.067
You know what, it was.

00:03:12.067 --> 00:03:13.664
That was very nice of you to do.

00:03:13.664 --> 00:03:15.652
Look at that, I'm paying you a compliment.

00:03:15.652 --> 00:03:17.733
That's a genuine compliment.

00:03:17.733 --> 00:03:19.492
This mustache sometimes can be used

00:03:19.492 --> 00:03:22.420
for me to do an impression of your father.

00:03:22.420 --> 00:03:24.003
Sona, Sona, please.

00:03:24.877 --> 00:03:26.231
Why don't you marry?

00:03:26.231 --> 00:03:27.814
Sona, Sona, please.

00:03:29.022 --> 00:03:30.161
Is that kind of what he's like?

00:03:30.161 --> 00:03:31.211
No not at all.

00:03:31.211 --> 00:03:34.041
A lot cooler than-- he
does have a mustache.

00:03:34.041 --> 00:03:34.999
And he is a cool guy.

00:03:34.999 --> 00:03:36.095
He's the coolest guy.

00:03:36.095 --> 00:03:38.138
But you gotta admit, if you just came

00:03:38.138 --> 00:03:41.649
across me quickly, you might
think this is your father.

00:03:41.649 --> 00:03:43.316
Sona, Sona, America.

00:03:44.397 --> 00:03:45.390
America.

00:03:45.390 --> 00:03:49.557
He's got a more like,
just human skin tone.

00:03:49.699 --> 00:03:50.532
That's rude.

00:03:50.532 --> 00:03:51.423
(laughter)

00:03:51.423 --> 00:03:52.623
Okay we have Marie.

00:03:52.623 --> 00:03:53.469
Marie, wave!

00:03:53.469 --> 00:03:54.302
You're way back there.

00:03:54.302 --> 00:03:55.729
I don't know if you can see Marie.

00:03:55.729 --> 00:03:59.657
Marie is Jeff Ross' assistant,
so she really has a job.

00:03:59.657 --> 00:04:01.227
She has things she has to do.

00:04:01.227 --> 00:04:02.687
She's constantly working cause Jeff

00:04:02.687 --> 00:04:04.343
actually works on the show.

00:04:04.343 --> 00:04:06.606
I'm a jackass and a
fool, and you enable me.

00:04:06.606 --> 00:04:08.873
And you're an enabler and
probably and alcoholic.

00:04:08.873 --> 00:04:10.629
(laughter)

00:04:10.629 --> 00:04:12.109
And so we have a good time.

00:04:12.109 --> 00:04:13.963
And here's your Wall-E, right here.

00:04:13.963 --> 00:04:16.254
This is Sona's probably only friend.

00:04:16.254 --> 00:04:18.671
(toy noises)

00:04:21.864 --> 00:04:23.139
And you're an adult.

00:04:23.139 --> 00:04:24.347
(laughter)

00:04:24.347 --> 00:04:25.847
Yes I am.

00:04:25.847 --> 00:04:28.491
I don't know, I think that
pretty much takes you through.

00:04:28.491 --> 00:04:31.025
Oh and this is Sona
trying way too hard to put

00:04:31.025 --> 00:04:32.889
her Armenian past behind her.

00:04:32.889 --> 00:04:34.222
She does this whenever people

00:04:34.222 --> 00:04:35.438
coming to ask for her green card.

00:04:35.438 --> 00:04:37.024
She's like, "America!"

00:04:37.024 --> 00:04:38.222
I was born here.

00:04:38.222 --> 00:04:39.055
Really?

00:04:39.055 --> 00:04:39.888
Not really

00:04:39.888 --> 00:04:41.589
Yeah, really I was born in this country.

00:04:41.589 --> 00:04:43.057
She washed up on shore here,

00:04:43.057 --> 00:04:44.662
and I found her in a bush.

00:04:44.662 --> 00:04:48.080
And taught her English by having her watch

00:04:48.080 --> 00:04:51.749
various soap operas on TV, Falcon's Crest.

00:04:51.749 --> 00:04:53.408
Okay, I'm gonna go.

00:04:53.408 --> 00:04:56.825
Sona why don't you enjoy this Korean beer

00:04:58.216 --> 00:04:59.853
that they've put my face on?

00:04:59.853 --> 00:05:01.501
My face is on everything here.

00:05:01.501 --> 00:05:02.334
It really is.

00:05:02.334 --> 00:05:03.192
Your life must be a hell.

00:05:03.192 --> 00:05:04.025
It is.

00:05:04.025 --> 00:05:04.858
Okay.

00:05:04.858 --> 00:05:05.807
That's us.
(clap)

00:05:05.807 --> 00:05:06.649
Peace out.

00:05:06.649 --> 00:05:07.482
Say Tupac.

00:05:08.356 --> 00:05:09.264
What?
I don't know.

00:05:09.264 --> 00:05:10.521
Isn't that a thing kids.
Say Tupac?

00:05:10.521 --> 00:05:12.016
I'm trying to be with the kids.

00:05:12.016 --> 00:05:13.308
Tupac.
Peace out.

00:05:13.308 --> 00:05:15.703
Yeah, or dear, or dear mama.

00:05:15.703 --> 00:05:18.363
Oh dear mama. (laughs)

00:05:18.363 --> 00:05:19.196
Oh my god.

